                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 06/07/2024 due to symptomatic aortic valve stenosis. On admission, clinical examination revealed signs consistent with severe aortic stenosis, including a systolic ejection murmur and reduced exercise tolerance. Diagnostic workup included echocardiography confirming severe aortic stenosis with significantly reduced valve area, supplemented by chest X-ray, ECG, and laboratory blood tests. Following interdisciplinary heart team discussion, the patient was deemed suitable for transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI). The procedure was performed successfully on 06/08/2024 without immediate complications. Post-procedural recovery was uneventful. Pharmacological management was adjusted accordingly, and the patient received discharge education. He is now stable and fit for discharge into your care. Please continue guideline-directed medical therapy and arrange follow-up echocardiography in 6–8 weeks.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
